# Tracer: complete-domain evidence for function graphs and spaces.
# Before on binary 98b5656c3fd7cefbfb01aa571b94023f5cb7ff3542f67011ebe1735b626130d3:
# $is_nonempty_set(fn(k {}) R {0})
# fn_range(fn(k {}) R {0})={0}
# Both false statements were accepted; empty image={} was not proved.
# Now: image emptiness consumes the checked complete domain. Nonempty
# graphs and singleton constant images retain actual inputs and guards.
# Empty-domain function spaces contain the empty function even with empty
# return carriers. Nonempty function spaces can contain returned functions.
# Boundary: empty graph nonemptiness and singleton-image claims are real
# negatives in examples/negative/exact_function_domains/manifest.json.
# Gate actually used: tmp/2026-10-05/tuple-cart-exact-functions/target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/function_empty_domain_graph.lit

fn_range(fn(k {}) R {0})={}

